WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.250 --> 00:00:06.500
The word solidarity appears 16 times in the
Treaties

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:12.031
Our European budget is living proof of financial
solidarity.

00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:15.530
The euro is an expression of solidarity.

00:00:15.530 --> 00:00:20.430
Our development policy is a strong external
sign of solidarity.

00:00:20.430 --> 00:00:27.359
And when it comes to managing the refugee
crisis, we have started to see solidarity.

00:00:27.359 --> 00:00:31.070
I am convinced much more solidarity is needed.

00:00:31.070 --> 00:00:38.000
But I also know that solidarity must be 
voluntary. It must come from the heart.

00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:41.500
It cannot be forced. It cannot be imposed.

00:00:42.500 --> 00:00:51.500
I am urging the Slovak Presidency to bridge the divergencies and differences between those who are

00:00:51.600 --> 00:00:59.000
reluctant to integrate refugees in their societies and those who are convinced, as I am, that the fair share

00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:04.500
in the relocation and resettlement is of the essence.

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:19.500
What I am asking is strong and immediate action both from Greece and the European Union

00:01:19.500 --> 00:01:26.000
to protect what we call in French les enfants non accompagnés.

00:01:26.000 --> 00:01:32.500
Without protection of these children, the European Union is betraying its historic values.

00:01:37.000 --> 00:01:41.479
In the 
same spirit, the Commission is proposing today

00:01:41.479 --> 00:01:45.590
to set up a European Solidarity Corps.

00:01:45.590 --> 00:01:52.520
Young people across the EU will be able to
volunteer their help where it is needed most,

00:01:52.520 --> 00:01:58.600
to respond to crisis situations, like the
refugee crisis or the recent earthquakes in Italy.

